koz VM : a literal next to a variable, on the right and on the left of every operator finkoz

zafer nombres(n)
ouver
    afise(n èk 5)
    afise(5 èk n)
    afise(n mwin 3)
    afise(3 mwin n)
    afise(n fwa 2)
    afise(2 fwa n)
    afise(n koup 4)
    afise(40 koup n)
fèrm
nombres(10)

koz comparisons : a literal on the left is turned around, 11 piti n means n dépas 11 finkoz
zafer comparaisons(n)
ouver
    afise(n piti 11)
    afise(11 piti n)
    afise(n pli-piti-egal 10)
    afise(10 pli-piti-egal n)
    afise(n dépas 9)
    afise(9 dépas n)
    afise(n plis-gran-egal 11)
    afise(11 plis-gran-egal n)
    afise(n parey 10)
    afise(10 parey n)
    afise(n diferan 10)
    afise(11 diferan n)
fèrm
comparaisons(10)

koz strings : concatenation keeps the order, equality does not care finkoz
zafer textes(s)
ouver
    afise(s èk "!")
    afise("> " èk s)
    afise(s parey "Lebon")
    afise("Lebon" parey s)
    afise(s diferan "autre")
fèrm
textes("Lebon")

koz two literals, a literal in a longer expression and a literal assigned to a variable finkoz
afise(2 fwa 3 èk 4)
afise(10 mwin 2 mwin 3)
afise(1 èk 2 piti 4)
keksoz total idon 7
total idon total fwa 3
afise(total)
